  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), giving a minimal baseline. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task at all. Question: config_010 (image-only, single-profile, ResNet-50) provides a clean, single-variable contrast to config_001—same profile setting (singleprofile), no aggregation or fusion—so the comparison isolates the effect of modality. Why this is the best next experiment: In a multimodal study, knowing the relative strength of each modality in isolation is the foundational decision that shapes every subsequent choice (which encoder to prioritize, whether fusion is worthwhile, whether multiprofile aggregation is needed). If image-only performs comparably or better than RNA-only, it justifies investing budget in multimodal fusion configurations; if it is much weaker, it redirects attention toward improving the RNA side (better encoders, multiprofile). This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty with a single clean comparison, avoiding the confound of simultaneously introducing a new modality, a new fusion strategy, and a new profile setting."
}

